    {
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "caption": "The kernel maps each PT_LOAD, sets up the brk, and maps the PT_INTERP too.",
      "narration": "It tears down the old address space and maps each PT_LOAD with the right permissions. If there's a PT_INTERP, such as ld-linux, it maps that interpreter as well.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "What load_elf_binary does",
